understand	From Middle English understanden, from Old English understandan ("to understand"), from Proto-West Germanic *understandan ("to stand between, understand"), from Proto-Germanic *understandaną ("to stand between, understand"), equivalent to Old English under- ("between, inter-") + standan ("to stand") (Modern English under- + stand). Cognate with Old Frisian understonda ("to understand, experience, learn"), Old High German understantan ("to understand"), Middle Danish understande ("to understand").
