undo	From Middle English undōn, from Old English ondōn, from Proto-West Germanic *andadōn ("to undo"), equivalent to un- + do. Cognate with West Frisian ûndwaan, ûntdwaan ("to undo; rid"), Dutch ontdoen ("to undo").
