unguent	Borrowed from Latin unguentum ("ointment"), from unguō ("to smear with ointment"), from Proto-Indo-European *h₃engʷ- ("to salve, anoint"). Cognates include Old Prussian anctan, Old High German ancho (German Anke ("butter")), Welsh ymenyn ("butter").
