unidentifiable	From un- + identifiable.
unidentified	From un- + identified.
unidentified_flying_object	The phrase is usually attributed to US Air Force officer Edward J. Ruppelt (1923-1960) who coined it as a replacement of the terms flying saucer and flying disk.
