unio	From the genus name, Unio, from Latin ūniō ("large pearl"). Doublet of union.
union	From Middle English unyoun, from Old French union, from Late Latin ūniō, ūniōnem ("oneness, unity"), from Latin ūnus ("one"). Doublet of unio.	(locomotive): Derived from the name of the only U.S. company to use that configuration.	Probably a variant spelling of Onion.
