unlax	Blend of unwind + relax?
unleaded	From un- + leaded. The US standard of identity comes from 40 CFR §79.32.
unlearn	From Middle English unlernen. By surface analysis, un- + learn.
unlearned	From Middle English unlerned ("not taught, uneducated"). By surface analysis, un- ("not") + learned ("educated").	From un- ("not") + learned ("studied"), past participle of learn.	From Middle English unlernyd ("obliterated from memory, forgotten"), equivalent to unlearn + -ed.
