unlikable	From un- + likable.
unlike	From Middle English unlic, unlich, from Old English unlīċ, unġelīċ ("unlike, different, dissimilar, diverse"), from Proto-Germanic *ungalīkaz. By surface analysis, un- + like. Cognate with Dutch ongelijk, German ungleich, Old Norse úlíkr (see there for North Germanic descendants).	From Middle English unliken, unlyken, equivalent to un- + like.
