untagged	From un- + tagged.
untainted	From un- + tainted.
untalented	From un- + talented.
untalkative	From un- + talkative.
untamed	From Middle English untamed, untemed, equivalent to un- + tamed and/or untame + -ed. Compare Dutch ongetemd ("untamed"), German ungezähmt ("untamed"), Danish utæmmet ("untamed"), Swedish otämd ("untamed"), Icelandic ótamin ("untamed").
untangle	From un- + tangle.
untanned	From un- + tanned.
untaped	See the etymology of the corresponding lemma form.	From un- + taped.
untapped	From un- + tapped.
untarnished	From un- + tarnished.
untasted	From un- + tasted.
untaught	From Middle English untauȝt; equivalent to un- + taught.
untaxed	From un- + taxed.
unteach	From un- + teach.
untechnical	From un- + technical.
untellable	From Middle English untellable; equivalent to un- + tellable.
