unthankful	From Middle English unthankful, from Old English unþancful, unþancfull, unġeþancfull ("unthankful, ungrateful"), equivalent to un- + thankful. Cognate with Old High German undankfol ("unthankful, ungrateful").
unthaw	From un- (intensifier) + thaw.
unthawed	From un- + thawed.	From unthaw + -ed.
untheatrical	From un- + theatrical.
unthematic	From un- + thematic.
